language variant
language en-gb-scotland
name sam
gender male 33

// A DISTINCT MOUTH FOR THE BETWEEN-VOICE.
// The base was plain `en`, which is the same unmarked English `classic` already
// speaks; two entries in a picker sharing an accent is two entries that sound
// like one. en-gb-scotland is a real, separate phoneme set on this host, and it
// is nobody else's here. The tuning below is untouched — the computed D3-G3
// fourth and the harshness loaded onto stress 5-7 are what makes this Sam; the
// accent only decides whose mouth says it.

// BETWEEN, ARRIVED AT RATHER THAN ASSERTED.
// The set already has a floor and a ceiling: leaderofearth speaks from E2
// (82.41 Hz), jaimla reaches C4 (261.63 Hz). The geometric mean of those two
// extremes is sqrt(82.41 x 261.63) = 146.8 Hz — which is D3 (146.83), and which
// lands within 2% of 150, the f0 NeuralVoiceEngine.js assigns to its explicitly
// gender-'neutral' profile (src/NeuralVoiceEngine.js:50-55). Sam's floor is
// literally the midpoint of the voices around it. Neutrality here is a computed
// position between this system's own poles, not a guess at an average human.
//
// The span is a perfect fourth, D3 to G3 (146.83 -> 196.00, a ratio of 4:3):
// wider than nothing, narrower than jaimla's fifth or leaderofearth's octave.
// The fourth is the interval that refuses to resolve as major or minor, which
// is the correct joke to make with a gender-neutral voice.
pitch 147 196

// Formants sit between the two sets on purpose: leaderofearth damps F1-F3 and
// jaimla lifts them, so Sam scales them ~108 — above the male set, below the
// female one, in the region the ear declines to sex.
formant 0 100 116 120
formant 1 108 116 116
formant 2 110 114 110
formant 3 108 108  98
formant 4 106 104  90
formant 5 102  98  76
formant 6  96  92  58
formant 7  92  88  46
formant 8  90  86  38

// Balanced low and mid, with deliberate presence at 2.6 kHz — the band the ear
// reads as edge and articulation. Kept moderate at rest; it is what the harsh
// register has to bite with.
tone 480 215 1200 205 2600 150

// APPEALING AT REST.
breath  1 2 3 3 3 3 3 2
breathw 90 120 130 130 130 130 120 100
voicing 72
consonants 74 66
flutter 1

// HARSH WHEN ADAMANT — and an honest account of how.
//
// A variant file is STATIC. It cannot detect anger; nothing here inspects the
// text. What it CAN choose is how emphasis manifests, and emphasis is exactly
// what insistence produces: espeak drives stress levels 6-7 on emphatic and
// adamant delivery, and leaves 0-3 for ordinary speech.
//
// So the harshness is loaded onto the TOP of the stress curve. Levels 0-4 are
// low and nearly flat, which is the appealing, level register Sam speaks in
// normally. Levels 5-7 climb steeply — 17, 26, 33 — and that jump is what turns
// edged and critical, because `roughness 2` only becomes audible when driven
// hard. The voice is not angry; it becomes harsh precisely when it insists,
// which is the closest a static formant voice can honestly get.
roughness 2
intonation 1
stressAmp   13 13 14 15 17 22 28 33
stressAdd    0  5 15 25 40 65 105 145
